\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Initial Jobless Claims Fell Last Week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paulo Trevisani \par \uc2 132 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 December 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The number of Americans who filed for new unemployment benefits declined last week, as the U.S. labor market faces heightened economic uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 In the week through Dec. 20, 214,000 new unemployment claims were filed, a decrease from 224,000 a week earlier, the Labor Department said Thursday. Economists polled by The Wall Street Journal had been forecasting 225,000 claims.\par \par \uc2 Claims filings have been fluctuating between 200,000 and 250,000 a week, on a seasonally adjusted basis, for most of this year, as employers have been reluctant to let go of workers in face of a hazy economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 Data delayed by the government shutdown and released last week showed unemployment rising to 4.6% last month.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich450\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6750
