\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Amtrak Workers to Get $900 Bonuses\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 248 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Unionized Amtrak workers will receive bonuses this holiday season, funded by top executives who agreed to give up half of their bonus packages and others who had long-term bonuses eliminated. A U.S. News article on Saturday about the bonuses incorrectly implied that 246 managers gave up half their bonuses.\par \par \uc2 (WSJ Dec. 17, 2025)\par \par \uc2 (END)\par \par \uc2 More than 18,000 unionized \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  workers will each get a $900 bonus this holiday season, funded by managers who agreed to give up half of their bonus.\par \par \uc2 Some 246 \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  managers agreed to forgo around $16.2 million of their bonus packages this year, the Transportation Department said Friday. \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 's board of directors voted to distribute the funds to unionized front-line workers.\par \par \uc2 The move is part of a larger effort by the Trump administration to rejigger \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 's bonus program for executives and managers.\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 's board has also eliminated long-term incentive bonuses for management. The Transportation Department said it would restructure the bonuses.\par \par \uc2 The national rail operator, a quasi-government agency, provides passenger service between cities. It operates more than 300 trains a day, covering routes across 46 states and the District of Columbia.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have in recent years criticized \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 's incentive pay as wasteful.\par \par \uc2 Sens. Ted Cruz (R., Texas) and \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  (R., Neb.) have attacked \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  for distributing large bonuses between fiscal years 2021 and 2023, though the railroad recorded billions of dollars in losses.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Trump administration said \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 's bonus program "resulted in exorbitant payouts for senior staff."\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  didn't respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 In the fiscal year that ended Sept. 30, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  set a record ridership with 34.5 million customers. It recorded a net loss of $1.76 billion.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251213elcd0001o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
