\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Palantir\uc2  Suit Alleges Rival Poached Staff --- The complaint says Percepta's CEO built a 'copycat' company after exiting \uc2 Palantir\b0\par\par\uc2 By Victoria Albert \par \uc2 673 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Palantir\uc2  is expanding its legal campaign against a rival artificial-intelligence company, accusing the CEO and two other employees of engaging in a sprawling effort to poach \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's workers and customers.\par \par \uc2 The data-analysis firm, co-founded by a group including \uc2 Alex Karp\uc2  and \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2 , said in a court filing that Percepta CEO and co-founder Hirsh Jain and co-founder Radha Jain (no relation) aggressively pursued \uc2 Palantir\uc2  employees for a "copycat" company, in violation of their nonsolicitation agreements. It accused a third employee, Joanna Cohen, of stealing confidential documents from \uc2 Palantir\uc2  before she left for the rival firm.\par \par \uc2 Percepta said that it has never used any of \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's confidential information and accused the company of cherry-picking out of context information, calling \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's case "baseless."\par \par \uc2 "Percepta's business is fundamentally different from \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's. \uc2 Palantir\uc2  does not own the AI transformation space, which is massive and constantly evolving," Percepta said in a statement shared by \uc2 General Catalyst\uc2 , which launched the company this year. "This is the latest in \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's effort to use fear tactics to bully ex-employees out of innovating with applied AI."\par \par \uc2 Hirsh Jain, Radha Jain and Cohen are all former \uc2 Palantir\uc2  employees. The document, filed Thursday in U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York, builds on a lawsuit \uc2 Palantir\uc2  filed against Radha Jain and Cohen in October.\par \par \uc2 "Defendants brazenly disregarded their contractual and legal commitments to \uc2 Palantir\uc2  and instead chose a path of deception and unjust competition -- a path they continue trundling down to this day, and that irreparably harms \uc2 Palantir\uc2  and their ex-colleagues," the company said in its Thursday filing.\par \par \uc2 Palantir\uc2  sells software to centralize, manage and analyze large quantities of data. It dived into the white-hot AI market with a surprise announcement from Karp in 2023 and has since become the mainstay data and AI contractor for the U.S. military, other government agencies and corporate customers. The \uc2 U.S. Navy\uc2  earlier this week said it awarded \uc2 Palantir\uc2  a contract valued at hundreds of millions of dollars to manage the supply chain of its nuclear submarine fleet.\par \par \uc2 The legal action is part of a wave of legal battles over trade secrets in the AI sector, with companies such as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's \uc2 xAI\uc2  suing ex-employees and competitors for alleged infractions. \uc2 Palantir\uc2  said Radha Jain and Cohen didn't publicly disclose that they had joined a rival firm until Percepta's launch in early October 2025.\par \par \uc2 Hirsh Jain recruited Radha Jain after he left \uc2 Palantir\uc2  in August 2024, according to the filing. The pair allegedly worked to recruit other \uc2 Palantir\uc2  employees, in violation of their nonsolicitation agreements. Radha Jain resigned from \uc2 Palantir\uc2  in November of that year.\par \par \uc2 The company said Percepta's workforce and founding team are now disproportionately composed of ex-\uc2 Palantir\uc2  employees. That was Hirsh Jain's intention, the filing said, citing an alleged text to Radha Jain in which he said: "I'm down to pillage the best devs at \uc2 Palantir\uc2  when they're at their maximum richness."\par \par \uc2 The filing also accused Radha Jain of working with Percepta to pitch a potential \uc2 Palantir\uc2  customer while still employed at the data-analysis firm. That customer signed with Percepta, the suit said, which has generated millions in revenue for the company.\par \par \uc2 Cohen, the filing said, sent herself a slate of highly confidential documents around the time of her resignation in March 2025. The filing further alleged she used her personal phone to take photographs of confidential information on her \uc2 Palantir\uc2  computer, in what the company called "an obvious effort to evade \uc2 Palantir\uc2 's data security systems."\par \par \uc2 Palantir\uc2  had previously leveled similar allegations against Cohen and accused Radha Jain of violating her noncompete. Attorneys for the pair said in a November legal filing that they deny the allegations. The pair temporarily agreed to stop work for Percepta while proceedings continue, according to the November filing.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251212elcc0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
