\par\par \b \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  Joins Push For 401(k) Annuities\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anne Tergesen \par \uc2 918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 December 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vanguard Group\uc2  plans to start letting workers buy an annuity within a new 401(k) target-date fund.\par \par \uc2 The nation's largest target-date fund provider will make the fund available to employers starting sometime in 2026. Like any target-date fund, it will combine stocks and bonds, shifting to a more-conservative mix as investors age. But it will also give older workers the option of moving some of their 401(k) savings into an annuity, an insurance contract that converts an upfront lump-sum payment into fixed monthly payments for life.\par \par \uc2 A 65-year-old worker nearing retirement with a $1 million portfolio might use 25% to pay for an annuity, which today could provide about $1,670 a month. The worker would also be able to withdraw from the rest of the 401(k) savings, which would remain in stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 The move by \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 , which manages about 40% of the $4.5 trillion in target-date funds, suggests that annuities embedded in diversified 401(k) investments are slowly moving into the mainstream. Target-date funds are typically the default investments when employers automatically enroll workers in 401(k) plans.\par \par \uc2 Until recently, employers have largely focused on helping workers accumulate larger 401(k) balances. But as baby boomers retire, they are adding products and services that aim to replicate pensions, which cover a dwindling share of the U.S. workforce.\par \par \uc2 As 401(k)s have surpassed pensions, "There is far less guaranteed income in retirement," said \uc2 Lauren Valente\uc2 , head of workplace solutions at \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 . Annuities provide a stream of income that is insulated from stock-market losses and can eliminate the risk of running out of money, she said.\par \par \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 's rivals including State Street Investment Management, \uc2 J.P. Morgan Asset Management\uc2  and \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  have also introduced target-date funds with annuities. Around 4% of 401(k) plans now offer such a fund, an option that wasn't widely available until the past couple of years, according to Callan, an investment-consulting firm.\par \par \uc2 Many employers are taking a wait-and-see approach to target-date funds with annuities because of their higher costs and complexities, said Greg Ungerman, Callan's defined-contribution practice leader.\par \par \uc2 Many employers find it hard to compare target-date funds that use different types of annuities, he said.\par \par \uc2 While retirement savers might be able to earn higher returns by leaving more of their money in the stock market, many prefer the security and predictability of annuities.\par \par \uc2 Higher interest rates since 2022 have raised annuity payments, because insurers are earning more on the bonds in which they mainly invest customers' cash.\par \par \uc2 Retirees who are considering an annuity should understand their fees and features, including when payments start, their size and whether you can get your money back.\par \par \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 's new target-date series, called the \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  Target Retirement Lifetime Income Trusts, lets workers put some of their savings into an annuity from \uc2 TIAA\uc2 , which has historically specialized in retirement plans for nonprofits and universities.\par \par \uc2 Starting at age 55 for workers, their target-date fund accounts begin allocating some money to a \uc2 TIAA\uc2  insurance contract, which replaces part of their bondholdings.\par \par \uc2 By 65, account owners would have about 25% of their savings in the \uc2 TIAA\uc2  Secure Income Account, which pays a guaranteed interest rate that is currently 4.05%, although long-term contributors get a higher rate.\par \par \uc2 Workers leaving their jobs have the ability to use some or all of their target-date fund balance to purchase a \uc2 TIAA\uc2  fixed annuity that starts payments immediately. Or they can leave the money in the fund and continue collecting guaranteed interest from \uc2 TIAA\uc2 , retaining the option to eventually annuitize if they want to, said Colbert Narcisse, chief product officer at \uc2 TIAA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors can't change their minds once the annuity's lifetime income has begun. They can elect to continue the income over a spouse's lifetime and add a death benefit for other heirs.\par \par \uc2 The annuity isn't inflation-adjusted, though \uc2 TIAA\uc2  has historically provided profit-sharing payments in some years.\par \par \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  currently charges 0.08% a year for its target-date funds. The cost for the new series with the annuity will become public closer to launch.\par \par \uc2 Fidelity Investments\uc2 , the second-largest manager of target-date funds, said it has no immediate plans to incorporate annuities into those products.\par \par \uc2 So far, annuity offerings in target-date funds have varied.\par \par \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 's LifePath Paycheck invests in group annuity contracts for participants ages 55 and older. By age 65, the contracts comprise about 30% of employees' assets. Between age 59<frac12> and 71, participants have the option to purchase a fixed annuity that begins payments immediately.\par \par \uc2 State Street's IncomeWise lets older workers put up to 25% of their nest egg into a deferred annuity that starts payments at age 78, providing a higher income than an immediate annuity.\par \par \uc2 AllianceBernstein\uc2  offers a target-date fund with a variable annuity, which provides some exposure to the stock market.\par \par \uc2 Retirees can cash out their balance at any time, canceling the annuity. The fee is about 1.25% a year.\par \par \uc2 T. Rowe Price Group\uc2  launched a fund in January for retirees that delivers a 7.5% payout rate on the balance invested, until deferred annuity payments start 15 years later.\par \par \uc2 Most of the funds, including \uc2 Vanguard\uc2 's, leave it up to older workers to buy the annuity. But some automate the annuity purchase unless the participant opts out.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251204elc40001i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
