\par\par \uc2 Technology & Media\par \b \uc2 Verizon\uc2  Begins Laying Off More Than 13,000 Workers --- CEO launches its largest-ever round of cuts with email to its U.S. employees\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patience Haggin \par \uc2 387 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Verizon Communications\uc2  began notifying employees on Thursday if they are affected by its largest-ever round of layoffs, the company's chief executive said in an all-staff email viewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  plans to lay off more than 13,000 employees as part of CEO \uc2 Dan Schulman\uc2 's plan to aggressively reduce the company's entire cost base. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  is facing fierce competition for wireless-service and home-internet customers, and Schulman said he plans to reverse a recent trend of customer losses.\par \par \uc2 "Our current cost structure limits our ability to invest significantly in our customer value proposition," Schulman wrote in the email. "We must reorient our entire company around delivering for and delighting our customers."\par \par \uc2 The Journal reported last week that the company was planning to cut roughly 15,000 jobs. \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's leadership scaled back its downsizing slightly since then, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 While U.S. employees being laid off were being notified on Thursday, some employees abroad may be informed of their status in coming weeks, the person said. Schulman said in the email that \uc2 Verizon\uc2  will significantly reduce its outsourced and outside labor expenses. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  had about 100,000 employees as of February, according to securities filings. Most aren't unionized. The layoffs will reduce \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's labor expenses for nonunion employees by about 20%, the person said.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's board named Schulman its new CEO last month after it soured on prior chief \uc2 Hans Vestberg\uc2 's network-first focus. Schulman, a former CEO of \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , was the board's lead independent director at the time.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  is the largest U.S. telecommunications provider by subscriber base. In the latest quarter, it lost a net 7,000 consumer postpaid phone connections. Wall Street analysts had forecast a gain of 19,000. \uc2 AT&T\uc2  and \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2  have both been growing postpaid subscriber counts.\par \par \uc2 In Thursday's email, Schulman announced a $20 million reskilling and career-transition fund for employees who are leaving, aimed at preparing them for the age of artificial intelligence. He also said the company will share further details about organizational restructuring in coming weeks.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich445\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6675
