\par\par \b \uc2 Verizon\uc2  Plans To Cut Workforce By 15% --- New CEO seeks big cost reductions after board soured on predecessor\b0\par\par\uc2 By Emily Glazer, Suzanne Vranica and Patience Haggin \par \uc2 1,043 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Verizon Communications\uc2  plans to cut about 15,000 jobs -- the largest ever for the carrier, which is looking to reduce costs as it contends with increased competition for customers, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The move comes after \uc2 Verizon\uc2  last month ousted its chief executive, \uc2 Hans Vestberg\uc2 , and named its lead independent director \uc2 Daniel Schulman\uc2  as its new CEO.\par \par \uc2 Schulman, a former CEO of \uc2 PayPal\uc2  and \uc2 Virgin Mobile USA\uc2 , has said he would aggressively reduce the company's costs and take steps to reverse the customer losses. "\uc2 Verizon\uc2  is at a critical inflection point," he said last month.\par \par \uc2 The cuts are set to take place in the next week, the people said. The majority of the reduction is expected to be made through layoffs. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  also plans to transition about 200 stores into franchised operations, which will shift employees off its payroll, one of the people said. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  currently employs about 100,000 people.\par \par \uc2 The leadership change, announced in early October, was abrupt for a company that had conducted a multiyear horse race before appointing Vestberg. Before he was elevated, there were only two other men who had served as sole CEO since the company was created by \uc2 Bell Atlantic\uc2 's 2000 merger with GTE.\par \par \uc2 In September, the \uc2 Verizon\uc2  board, gathered at the carrier's Texas office, was losing patience with Vestberg, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  had reported two consecutive quarters of losses of core consumer wireless customers and was headed for a third. Rival \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2 , strengthened by its merger with \uc2 Sprint\uc2 , was strapped with valuable airwaves that made its often lower-cost service increasingly robust.\par \par \uc2 Vestberg wanted to continue pursuing a network-first strategy focused on ensuring that \uc2 Verizon\uc2  could tout the strength of its service. The company had put claims about its network's muscle at the center of its marketing efforts since its "Can you hear me now?" campaign in the early 2000s.\par \par \uc2 But the majority of \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's board wanted faster customer growth, especially ahead of a potential investor presentation in the works, according to people familiar with the matter. The board decided to tap one of \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's directors, Schulman, to take over.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  needs to become scrappier and less bureaucratic, Schulman said at a Wall Street Journal Leadership Institute event this week. "I'm not afraid at this point in my life to make really hard decisions," he said.\par \par \uc2 Some board members had questioned Vestberg's leadership over the prior two years though other candidates the company considered elevating hadn't panned out.\par \par \uc2 Some \uc2 Verizon\uc2  directors advocated giving Vestberg until year-end for a smooth CEO transition and not moving forward with the potential investor event, the people said. Others felt waiting could threaten the company's credibility if Vestberg presented to investors and a few months later \uc2 Verizon\uc2  announced a CEO change, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Days after the September board meeting, Vestberg was told he was out as CEO. Vestberg, who spent 28 years at \uc2 Ericsson\uc2 , including seven as its CEO, was also suddenly ousted from that top job after slumping sales and profits.\par \par \uc2 Schulman took over and board member \uc2 Mark Bertolini\uc2  was elected chairman.\par \par \uc2 Bertolini and Schulman had been among the most vocal of board members advocating for immediate change -- and splitting the chair and CEO roles -- even though some other directors weren't convinced the moves were necessary, some of the people said.\par \par \uc2 "The board needed to act and we acted," Bertolini told CNBC on Thursday. \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's network isn't as differentiated as it used to be, he said. "We have to do something different," he said.\par \par \uc2 One of Schulman's main challenges: Stoking new customer growth in a crowded U.S. market. Pricing competition with \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2  and \uc2 AT&T\uc2 , where he spent 18 years, is fierce.\par \par \uc2 Soon after his appointment, Schulman began holding meetings and firing off emails to staff.\par \par \uc2 He said at the Journal event this week that \uc2 Verizon\uc2  must pivot from being network engineering focused to being "obsessed with what customers want."\par \par \uc2 Vestberg had pursued deals to expand \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's network during his tenure, including prepaid-cellular provider \uc2 TracFone\uc2 , more than $50 billion in spectrum to support ultrafast 5G service and the roughly $20 billion purchase of \uc2 Frontier Communications\uc2 , a fiber internet provider. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  had also continued to raise prices until instituting a three-year price lock for some products in early 2025.\par \par \uc2 Schulman said Vestberg had done a good job getting \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's network to where it needed to be, but the next phase was about "customer centricity."\par \par \uc2 In the month Schulman has been on the job, he said he has written "three pretty lengthy memos" to the board about what he is seeing at the company and changes he is making.\par \par \uc2 "We have not performed for our shareholders. We have lost market share, consistently. And that cannot continue, going forward," Schulman said at the WSJ event.\par \par \uc2 The company shed a net 7,000 consumer postpaid phone connections in the September quarter, missing expectations that it would add 19,000 such customers. Schulman has said the company won't rush into cutting prices, but will look to find other ways to create value for customers.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  shares are down more than 30% over the past five years.\par \par \uc2 The new CEO has limited time to turn the company around. \uc2 Verizon\uc2 's contract with Schulman, 67 years old, runs through 2027, offering a $1.5 million base salary, plus tens of millions of dollars of various stock awards tied to the company's share performance and strength relative to peers.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  offered one-time $4 million retention equity awards to \uc2 Sowmyanarayan Sampath\uc2 , head of the carrier's consumer group, and finance chief \uc2 Anthony Skiadas\uc2  to retain them through at least the end of 2027.\par \par \uc2 Vestberg was given a year-long advisory role. At least one board member was adamant that the departing CEO should be eligible to receive the bulk of his compensation package, people familiar with the discussion said.\par \par \uc2 Vestberg is eligible for much of his more than $20 million pay package, subject to meeting certain goals.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich341\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal5115
