\par\par \b \uc2 Musk's Record Pay Plan Approved At \uc2 Tesla\uc2  --- Investors vote in favor of $1 trillion package after CEO threatened to quit\b0\par\par\uc2 By Becky Peterson \par \uc2 908 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  shareholders approved a record-setting pay package for Chief Executive \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , a plan designed to motivate the world's richest man with as much as $1 trillion in additional stock.\par \par \uc2 Flanked by dancing humanoid robots on a stage bathed in pink and blue lights at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's Austin, Texas headquarters, Musk thanked the crowd of shareholders who supported the pay package with more than 75% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 "What we're about to embark upon is not merely a new chapter of the future of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  but a whole new book," Musk said. "I guess what I'm saying is hang onto your \uc2 Tesla\uc2  stock," he said later.\par \par \uc2 The measure was hotly debated with some large shareholders taking opposing sides. The voting was largely seen as a referendum on \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's longtime leader and his vision to shift the electric-vehicle maker's focus to humanoid robots and artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Musk, who is also CEO of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 xAI\uc2 , had threatened on social media to leave \uc2 Tesla\uc2  if the measure was rejected. He is \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's biggest shareholder with a roughly 15% stake.\par \par \uc2 Musk had said he wanted a big enough ownership stake in \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to be comfortable that the "robot army" he was developing didn't fall into the wrong hands, but not so large that he couldn't be fired if he went "crazy."\par \par \uc2 On another proposal that would authorize the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  board to invest in Musk's artificial-intelligence company, \uc2 xAI\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  General Counsel \uc2 Brandon Ehrhart\uc2  said more shares had been voted for the nonbinding proposal than against, but there were many abstentions. He said the board would consider its next steps.\par \par \uc2 Musk had publicly endorsed the idea as he seeks to catch-up in the AI race.\par \par \uc2 The new pay package, which includes 12 chunks of stock, could give Musk control over as much as 25% of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  if he hits a series of milestones and expands the company's market capitalization to $8.5 trillion over the next 10 years. Its market cap is now around $1.5 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's board described the package as pay for performance, designed to encourage Musk to transform the company with new products such as autonomous vehicles, robotaxis and humanoid robots.\par \par \uc2 "Having worked with him now for 11 years, I can say what motivates him is doing things that others can't do or haven't been able to do," \uc2 Tesla\uc2  Chair \uc2 Robyn Denholm\uc2  said in an interview last week.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  struggled to keep Musk's attention earlier this year as he spent time in Washington running the \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2 . \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's vehicle sales fell more than 13% in the first half of the year. After Musk left Washington in May, he turned his focus to his startup \uc2 xAI\uc2  and the development of its chatbot Grok, The Wall Street Journal reported.\par \par \uc2 The new pay package was opposed by several proxy advisers and institutional investors including \uc2 California Public Employees' Retirement System\uc2 , the New York City retirement systems, and \uc2 Norges Bank Investment Management\uc2 , which is the sixth largest institutional shareholder with a 1.2% stake.\par \par \uc2 Institutional Shareholder Services\uc2 , one of the proxy advisers that urged passive funds to vote down the compensation package, said it had concerns about the magnitude and design of the "astronomical" stock award.\par \par \uc2 Charles Schwab\uc2 , which has a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  stake of about 0.6%, said on Tuesday that it would vote in favor of the package.\par \par \uc2 "We firmly believe that supporting this proposal aligns both management and shareholder interests," it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Huge stock awards tied to ambitious targets, sometimes called "moonshot" pay packages, are cast by proponents as a high-octane incentive for outstanding performance. Critics said they are often doubly flawed: overly expensive if targets prove easier than predicted -- and counterproductive if the targets become unattainable and executives see little reason to stick around.\par \par \uc2 Musk's new package is divided into 12 tranches. He could reach the first tranche if \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's market cap grows to $2 trillion from around $1.5 trillion today, combined with an operational goal such as selling 11.5 million new vehicles, on top of the 8.5 million vehicles on the road.\par \par \uc2 More challenging milestones include selling one million robots to paying customers and maintaining an adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, or Ebitda, of $400 billion. Last year, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  posted an adjusted Ebitda of $16 billion, down from a peak of $19 billion in 2022. By comparison in their last fiscal years, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  reported Ebitda of $18.7 billion and \uc2 Apple\uc2 , the most profitable U.S. company, reported nearly $145 billion.\par \par \uc2 For each tranche he unlocks, Musk would receive equity equivalent to about 1% of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's current shares. Once he earns a tranche, he could vote those shares but wouldn't be able to sell them until they vest, in either 7.5 years or 10 years.\par \par \uc2 Musk's 2018 pay package, the most valuable on record before the 2025 package, is tied up in a dispute at the Delaware Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is appealing a lower court decision to rescind the 2018 pay package after a judge ruled in January 2024 that \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's directors were beholden to Musk and the approval process for that package was tainted and lacked transparency.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich581\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal8715
