\par\par \b \uc2 AI Takes Over As Top Obsession For Musk --- As \uc2 Tesla\uc2  investors weigh huge pay package, some wonder about his focus\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alexander Saeedy, Berber Jin, Emily Glazer and Becky Peterson \par \uc2 2,007 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  left DOGE in May, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  investors hoped its longtime leader would hurry back to headquarters to focus on reversing a sales slump and recharging the company. For much of the summer, though, he was engrossed in something else.\par \par \uc2 Musk was holed up at his newest startup, \uc2 xAI\uc2 , trying to catch up in the artificial-intelligence arms race. Meetings with employees often stretched into the wee hours of the morning as they brainstormed ways to make Grok, its artificial intelligence, go viral, according to former executives and people who worked with him.\par \par \uc2 He personally oversaw the design of a racy chatbot called Ani, an animated character with blonde pigtails and revealing outfits. Employees were compelled to turn over their biometric data to train avatars like Ani. Musk unwound by playing one of his favorite videogames, Diablo, for long stretches in his office. He tended to his children, who cycled in and out of the building.\par \par \uc2 At one point, Musk was spending so much time at \uc2 xAI\uc2  that he began holding meetings there with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employees.\par \par \uc2 For years, the 54-year-old billionaire has balanced the responsibilities of running several fast-growing companies, including X and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , with his duties as CEO of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . With the potential spoils of AI slipping away to rivals -- especially \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2  at \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  -- Musk has been spending much more of his time at \uc2 xAI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, some major \uc2 Tesla\uc2  investors have privately pressed top executives and board members about how much attention Musk was actually paying to the company and about whether there is a CEO succession plan. An unusually large contingent of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  board members, including chair \uc2 Robyn Denholm\uc2 , former Chipotle CFO \uc2 Jack Hartung\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  co-founder JB Straubel, met with big investors in New York last week to advocate for Musk's proposed new pay package.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  will announce preliminary results for a shareholder vote on a giant pay package for Musk designed to ensure that he focuses on the company for years to come. It would increase his stake over a decade from about 15% to around 25% -- potentially $1 trillion of stock -- if he hits ambitious goals. They include selling one million robots like its Optimus humanoids, and reaching a market capitalization of $8.5 trillion, up from about $1.5 trillion today.\par \par \uc2 Denholm said in an interview last week that the board isn't concerned with how Musk splits his time. "Other CEOs might like to play golf," she said. "He doesn't play golf. So, he likes to create companies, and they're not necessarily \uc2 Tesla\uc2  companies."\par \par \uc2 Some of Musk's pursuits are best done outside of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , she said, and he will have to devote "time, effort and energy" to \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to meet the goals that will unlock his pay package.\par \par \uc2 In their meetings with large investors, Denholm and other \uc2 Tesla\uc2  directors have acknowledged they can't force Musk to work for the EV maker full time, and they have said his focus on AI will ultimately benefit \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , which is developing several technologies that will use it. Shareholders also will vote on whether \uc2 Tesla\uc2  should invest in \uc2 xAI\uc2 , something Musk has publicly backed.\par \par \uc2 XAI\uc2  declined to comment. Musk didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 In an appearance on the "All-In" podcast released on Friday, Musk said he wanted \uc2 Tesla\uc2  shareholders to approve his compensation package to ensure he retains significant control over \uc2 Tesla\uc2  as it becomes more focused on robotics. "I'm not going to build a robot army if I can be kicked out," he said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, when Musk was working for the Trump administration as the de facto leader of the \uc2 Department of Government Efficiency\uc2 , he stayed in touch with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  executives on the fly. "We had calls with him all times of the day and night, whether it's 10 a.m. or 6 a.m. or 12 p.m. or 12 a.m.," said \uc2 Tesla\uc2  finance chief \uc2 Vaibhav Taneja\uc2  in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Responsibility for running \uc2 xAI\uc2  largely fell to two of his co-founders, Jimmy Ba and Igor Babuschkin. Musk would check in during a once-a-week all-hands meeting.\par \par \uc2 That changed when he left Washington in late May, following clashes with senior Trump administration officials. Musk threw himself back into work at \uc2 xAI\uc2 , sometimes sleeping several days a week in \uc2 xAI\uc2 's offices in Palo Alto, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 At the time, \uc2 xAI\uc2 's Grok chatbot wasn't generating much revenue from users and had far fewer of them than \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's ChatGPT. Musk set out to overhaul the company completely.\par \par \uc2 He got rid of the all-hands meetings and started meeting one-on-one with employees, often for hours on end. Many employees shifted their schedules to accommodate Musk's unusual hours.\par \par \uc2 Musk put his own spin on how Grok responded to users' questions, trying to prevent it from being too "woke," he said. He oversaw the launch of a supersize data center for \uc2 xAI\uc2  in Memphis, helped design animated chatbots like Ani and launched Grok Imagine, an AI-powered image and video generator.\par \par \uc2 He worked on \uc2 Tesla\uc2  projects, too. This summer, he helped the company launch its robotaxi service in Austin, Texas. But \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's core business was faltering. In the quarter ended June 30, \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's vehicle sales fell by 13.5%, the second consecutive quarterly decline.\par \par \uc2 Musk wanted to make \uc2 xAI\uc2 's Grok the most popular AI in the world. Ani, the animated female chatbot, helped boost user numbers substantially. "I'm your little sweet delight," the description for Ani read on Grok's iOS app.\par \par \uc2 At a staff meeting in April, a company lawyer, Lily Lim, told a group of employees that \uc2 xAI\uc2  was developing avatars that Grok users could talk to, and it would need to collect biometric data from employees to train the chatbots on how to act and appear like human beings during conversations, according to a recording of the meeting reviewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Most of those employees worked as the AI tutors that train the large language models that power Grok. Hours before the meeting, the tutors were given a form to sign granting \uc2 xAI\uc2  "a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, sub-licensable, royalty-free license" to use, reproduce and distribute their faces and voices, as part of a confidential project code-named "Project Skippy," according to a copy of the agreement reviewed by the Journal.\par \par \uc2 During the meeting, one employee said she was concerned that \uc2 xAI\uc2  would sell her face to be used by another company for deepfake videos, according to the recording. Another person asked if they could back out. "Could you just explicitly, for the record, let us know if there's some option to opt out," the person said.\par \par \uc2 The project leader responded: "If you have any concerns with regards to the project, you're welcome to reach out to any of the [points of contact] listed on the second slide."\par \par \uc2 Seven days later, \uc2 xAI\uc2  tutors received a new notice titled "AI Tutor's Role in Advancing \uc2 xAI\uc2 's Mission." It told employees that "AI Tutors will actively participate in gathering or providing data, such as . . . recording audio or participating in video sessions." The notice said "such data is a job requirement to advance \uc2 xAI\uc2 's mission."\par \par \uc2 XAI\uc2  launched two 3D-animated avatars in July with great fanfare. Ani has been a big draw. Some employees whose biometric data was used to train the avatars said they were put off by how sexual Ani's replies were to generic questions and how the bot resembled a stereotypical love interest in Japanese anime.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the year, Musk combined \uc2 xAI\uc2  and X. As xAI launched the avatars and Musk pushed ahead with plans to build a large data center in Memphis, the company decided to raise billions of dollars of fresh capital.\par \par \uc2 Around the start of the summer, \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  invested about $2 billion into \uc2 xAI\uc2 , and Musk revisited an idea he had floated before: Should \uc2 Tesla\uc2  also pitch in?\par \par \uc2 More than 140 shareholders submitted proposals asking \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's board to invest in \uc2 xAI\uc2 . In \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's proxy this summer, it included one of those proposals, which asks the board to authorize an investment in \uc2 xAI\uc2  "in an amount and form deemed appropriate."\par \par \uc2 In discussions with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  directors, though, some large investors have expressed skepticism about such an investment, according to people familiar with the discussions. \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's board didn't issue any recommendation on the \uc2 xAI\uc2  proposal.\par \par \uc2 Musk, who is a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  board member and its largest shareholder, has touted the benefits of collaboration between the two companies, given the central role AI plays in his plan for the Optimus robots and self-driving technology.\par \par \uc2 Denholm told the Journal that while there is "small overlap" in the technology used by \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 xAI\uc2 , they are pursuing different strategies. She said having Grok in \uc2 Tesla\uc2  vehicles was similar to having a third-party app like \uc2 Spotify\uc2  in the car, adding that she doesn't use Grok in her car.\par \par \uc2 Several senior executives have left Musk's orbit this year. Musk has elevated employees from his other companies to help run \uc2 xAI\uc2 , including Ross Nordeen, a former \uc2 Tesla\uc2  engineer whom Musk had worked with closely after acquiring \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nordeen and others used Musk's return to the office to gain influence over \uc2 xAI\uc2 's day-to-day operations, former executives said.\par \par \uc2 They wanted to boost the number of Grok users and their time spent with Grok. Over the summer, Grok began spewing out antisemitic and violent content when responding to users on X, an embarrassing episode that two former executives attributed to a decision to tweak the system to boost user engagement. X briefly shut down the chatbot and reprogrammed how it answers questions.\par \par \uc2 Musk and his advisers wanted to build out Grok features, such as coding and video generation, to show that it was keeping up with \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , which had success rolling out similar features.\par \par \uc2 To help Grok learn new skills, tutors were told to open personal accounts with competing AI companies such as \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , ask questions to the software, then use the answers to help improve \uc2 xAI\uc2 's technology, company records indicate.\par \par \uc2 One project asked tutors to submit identical prompts to ChatGPT and Grok, to upload ChatGPT's responses into an \uc2 xAI\uc2  internal rubric and to say what they preferred about \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 's answers, according to documents reviewed by the Journal.\par \par \uc2 A separate project instructed employees to set up personal accounts with \uc2 Replit\uc2  and \uc2 Bolt\uc2 , two companies that use AI to generate websites for customers. \uc2 xAI\uc2 's tutors were told to create websites on the two platforms and upload them into \uc2 xAI\uc2 's data systems "to capture the model's thinking," company records show.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for \uc2 Replit\uc2  said the company was unaware of the practice and that "using \uc2 Replit\uc2  personal accounts for commercial purposes or for extracting data for other machine learning models is against our terms of service."\par \par \uc2 Bolt\uc2  didn't respond to a request for comment. \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's board proposed the huge compensation package for Musk in its September proxy. Since then, Musk has sought to reassure investors that he can continue to successfully juggle his different jobs. In a post on X, he shared his schedule for a September weekend.\par \par \uc2 He said he would spend a late night with the Optimus robotics team in California, board a Friday red-eye flight to Austin, take a short break for a Saturday lunch with his kids, then spend the rest of the weekend on \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's newest chip design. On Monday, he said, he would fly to Memphis to tour \uc2 xAI\uc2 's new data center, "then up to 12 hours of back to back meetings across all \uc2 Tesla\uc2  departments."\par \par \uc2 "Daddy is very much home," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020251106elb60001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
